From 3ba638c867251b3e79d18811de3265da071def59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 01:49:46 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] STD: hook select_task_rq

Hook select_task_rq via std_select_cpu. Keeps routing above deadline
with no new class. Respects affinity and small-system guard; pinned,
migrating, core (rq-wide, may over-skip) and EXT pass through, stop
never intercepted. Placement stays at wakeup time; the pick path is
untouched so the disabled cost is near-zero. Steering is best-effort
soft hint without guarantee.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
---
 kernel/sched/core.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/core.c b/kernel/sched/core.c
index 1754d9f95..6e9cff552 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/core.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/core.c
@@ -3634,6 +3634,14 @@ int select_task_rq(struct task_struct *p, int cpu, int *wake_flags)
 
 	if (p->nr_cpus_allowed > 1 && !is_migration_disabled(p)) {
 		cpu = p->sched_class->select_task_rq(p, cpu, *wake_flags);
+		/*
+		 * STD routing shim above deadline: steer toward the
+		 * preferred group best-effort soft hint without guarantee,
+		 * honoring affinity; stop never intercepted, pinned/migrating/
+		 * core(rq-wide, may over-skip)/EXT pass through. Wakeup only;
+		 * pick untouched.
+		 */
+		cpu = std_select_cpu(p, cpu);
 		*wake_flags |= WF_RQ_SELECTED;
 	} else {
 		cpu = cpumask_any(p->cpus_ptr);
-- 
